  "result": "The quote now prints `27.06`. The 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded a one-digit fraction on the wrong side. It used `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"12.5\"` became 12.05 (1205 cents) instead of 12.50 (1250 cents). I changed it to `ljust`, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`.\n\nI didn't add a test for one-decimal amounts like `12.5`, so nothing in the suite covers this case yet.",
